alked about earlier should  prevent you from being affected by the  gas clouds as shown in this clip I was  in there for a pretty decent time and  didn't get affected whatsoever yes it  does drain the vitality mentals health  bar a little bit but you are getting  some decent hits in as well another move  he'll do is what I called the head swing  it's pretty simple I'm pretty basic  he basically swipes his head on the  floor in front of him he basically goes  from right to left or left to right so  either way be far away from him or  behind him to avoid the move those are  the moves he'll be throwing at you  throughout the fight so let's get into  the areas so the area I started on is  mostly this land area with a tiny  electric pool in the back there isn't  much here except the entrance to his  nest is off to the right and you can use  the little ledge to mount and the mini  slope leading from the entrance to use  any sliding attacks reppin has he also  when he tries to limp to his nest he  will go around toward the electric area  do not follow that you you will get  blocked by an invisible wall and you  will take damage from the water just go  through the normal entrance as if you  were just going the regular way and you  should be completely fine like I said  you can use that mini slope leading from  his entrance to do any sliding attacks  your weapon has now I'm not entirely  versed on every single weapon in monster  hunter world I do use dual blades  basically 100% of the time and I do know  that they have a sliding move which is  very very deadly and very elegant  now I'm not entirely sure every weapon  has a type of sliding animation but if  it does have one you can use that mini  slope to do any sliding moves and get  some extra damage on him  so definitely utilize that while you can  the next area is also going to be an  area surrounded by the electric water  with some water  as well in the middle next to some  ledges this area is also pretty useless  except another ledge like I said by the  middle water source which can be used  for mounting as well and some no berries  around the edges toward the water if you  need some the third area though is  actually one of the areas you fight the  RO de the odo Garin which is that  bleeding monster somewhere in the rotten  Vale there will be some gear O's there  as well too they would usually get in  your way but if you're lucky Ken  paralyzed Vall and knock him over to  give you some free hits I wasn't able to  record it because my footage got  corrupted but trust me it did happen one  time and you will get some free hits  from it and then the last area is his  nest  it does have some water on the side so  also watch out for that and some gears  at the top and a slope of dead bodies  which is the entire thing he's resting  on you can also slide down that for a  possible mount and that's it you have  all the tools utilized to fight Valle  you have his weaknesses every single  thing about the weapons you should be  using where to hit him in the areas in  which you fight him in I hope you guys  did enjoy that video if you guys did it  please try to give it a like really does  help me out I have tons of these guys  coming I did beat all the bosses so far  except the last one which I don't want  to spoil the ending boss I did beat but  there's one all the way up in a hunter  rank 50 just in case for anybody that  doesn't want spoilers I won't say  anything but there is a boss that is  only accessible up at that point but  I've beaten all the main story bosses so  I'm gonna be working on the other two  other dragons and then the final boss as  well getting the videos out hopefully in  the last couple weeks of it you guys can  enjoy those but like I said if you guys  did enjoy the video please sure to give  it a like subscribe if you're new I post  a lot of Monster Hunter World content  like solo guides tons of news and tips  and all that type of stuff regarding  Monster Hunter World 